#!/usr/bin/env bash
# The ok-planner family's deterministic converge core — the conventional
# administration file the suite's front door (/ok) drives. The judgment
# the modes below cannot encode (overlapping project context, the
# drafts a cleanup offer needs) lives beside this script in
# ADMINISTRATION.md.
#
# - Resolves the project root: nearest ancestor of $PWD carrying an
#   estate marker (current or pre-migration), else $PWD — never derived
#   from .git.
# - mkdir -p's the .ok-planner/ subdirectory tree (including the
#   issues/ intake and history/issues/ archive; issues are one
#   markdown file each, never touched here).
# - Overwrites .ok-planner/CLAUDE.md and the cheatsheet from the
#   canonical templates in ../scripts (suite-owned boilerplate,
#   no merge, no diff), stamping the suite version into the
#   {{OK_PLANNER_VERSION}} placeholder so diagnose can detect staleness.
# - Materializes this family's ceremony contributions into
#   .ok-planner/ceremony/ — the conventional contributions the suite's
#   hoisted audit and documentation verbs drive. Every file the estate
#   carries is tracked content, so the estate needs no ignore file of
#   its own.
# - Materializes the review loop's estate: the review tool into
#   .ok-planner/bin/review, the directory note and catalog/ into
#   .ok-planner/review/ (overwritten), and config.json and project.md
#   seeded into .ok-planner/review/ only when absent — the owner's
#   after that. Moves a pre-move .ok-review/ estate into it.
# - Materializes the family LICENSE at the estate root and in every
#   vendored skill folder, each under a scope preamble naming Fall Guy
#   LLC and saying which files the grant covers — the estate root and
#   .claude/skills/ both hold project-owned content beside the
#   materialized files, and a bare license there would over-claim.
# - Materializes the session-start hook into .ok-planner/hooks/
#   (version-stamped, executable). The hook executes via a consented
#   entry in .claude/settings.json — see wire-hooks below — never from
#   the carried payload copy.
# - Vendors this family's own user-facing skills into .claude/skills/
#   (every .md under each skill folder, version-stamped, sibling
#   references rewritten to the materialized names). The audit and
#   documentation verbs are not among them: they belong to the suite,
#   and the suite's own converge core vendors them. A vendored path
#   holding the project's own unstamped file is a collision: offered,
#   never written over.
# - Vendors the task tracker's agent profiles (agents/ok-*.md) into
#   .claude/agents/, version-stamped: the files that pin each dispatch's
#   model and effort, which the drain names by subagent type.
# - Retires payloads earlier versions materialized (the skills-index
#   context payload, the user-prompt-submit hook now owned by the
#   ok-conduct plugin, the merged true-up verb the front door's
#   administration replaced, the retired prove and browse verbs, the
#   proof cost recorder with its machine-local record, the retired
#   corpus view — its service, its placed build, the run state it
#   recorded, and the estate ignore file that covered them — and the
#   committed source graph with its extractor).
# - Migrates retired layout on sight: specs/ from the spec era and
#   backlogs/ from before the backlog -> sprint rename move into
#   sprints/, plans/, coverage/, and design/review-notes*.md into
#   history/, and decision Proof sections from the retired
#   proof-mandate model are stripped.
# - Offers what it cannot settle alone as CLEANUP OFFERED blocks, each
#   naming what is there, the fix, and the consent command that applies
#   it: a collision, a retired verb the project wrote, a project rule
#   file the suite now carries, a review-estate conflict, an old catalog
#   edit, an entry whose migration path is taken, and — with a draft the
#   administrator writes — project.md wording, a legacy issues.jsonl,
#   pre-4.0 tensions, and a malformed or closed issue in the intake.
# - `converge diagnose` is the read-only mode: it reports missing
#   layout, stale or missing materialized files, retired layout, the
#   cleanup offers, and missing or drifted hook wiring (with the exact
#   entry to restore), and writes nothing. It exits 0 when clean, 1 on
#   anything converge or wire-hooks would change, and 3 when only
#   cleanup offers await the owner's word.
# - `converge wire-hooks` is the consent-transcription path — the ONLY
#   path that writes .claude/settings.json. Run it exactly when the
#   owner has consented to the entry diagnose reported as needed.
# - `converge resolve <id> [<choice>|--from <draft>]` applies the one
#   fix a CLEANUP OFFERED block names, on the owner's consent. It
#   re-reads the offers first and refuses an id diagnose would not
#   report now, a draft that changes what the offer keeps, and any
#   path that carries uncommitted work or sits behind a symbolic link.
#   Deletions go through plain `git rm` where git tracks the path.
#
# Idempotent. Re-running converge on a project already in compliance
# is a no-op at the git level.
#
# @decision: vendored-skills

set -euo pipefail

MODE="converge"
case "${1:-}" in
    diagnose) MODE="diagnose" ;;
    wire-hooks) MODE="wire-hooks" ;;
    resolve) MODE="resolve" ;;
esac

